From 7db1c33adefebd83c708fe54f46dd3d5e0dee365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:46:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 040/143] ksmbd: safely drain sessions during logoff

SMB3 multichannel allows requests for one session to run on multiple
connections. Wait for all channels bound to a session before freeing
shared session objects.

A deferred byte-range lock remains counted as a running request and only
wakes when its file closes. Wake blocked locks during the drain without
unpublishing or modifying their file objects. Synchronous CANCEL requests
must invoke their cancellation callback to wake pending operations, while
CHANGE_NOTIFY completion remains specific to the asynchronous path.

Serialize session teardown with channel registration and previous-session
cleanup, and use atomic work-state transitions so LOGOFF, CANCEL, and
connection teardown invoke cancellation callbacks only once.

Fixes: 76e98a158b20 ("ksmbd: fix race condition between destroy_previous_session() and smb2 operations()")
Reported-by: Cheryl Babcock <cheryl@renat.io>
Signed-off-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
[ Backport note: hand-written for 6.18 without the upstream prerequisites
  4b706360ffb7 (register_session_channel), c50e628122ae
  (ksmbd_conn_wait_idle_sess / ksmbd_session_is_bound_to_conn),
  4fd5bad647bf (ksmbd_conn_cancel_async_requests), 152036e875e8 /
  a47634cd729b (CHANGE_NOTIFY cancel claim, kerberos_expiry).
  Taken as upstream: sess->tearing_down serialised by chann_lock in
  smb2_session_logoff() and destroy_previous_session(), draining all
  session channels before ksmbd_close_session_fds() and tree teardown
  (replacing ksmbd_conn_wait_idle(conn)), the logoff error/rollback paths,
  ksmbd_wake_session_blocked_works() called from the drain loop, xchg()
  in set_close_state_blocked_works(), cmpxchg() in both smb2_cancel()
  paths and cancel_fn invocation for synchronous CANCEL.
  Adapted: 6.18 has no register_session_channel(), so the tearing_down
  check is done at the two open-coded channel xa_store() sites in
  ntlm_authenticate() and krb5_authenticate(). ksmbd_conn_wait_idle_sess_id()
  becomes ksmbd_conn_wait_idle_sess(conn, sess) with the 6.18 connection
  match (conn->binding || conn->sessions) plus sess->ksmbd_chann_list
  membership; ksmbd_all_conn_set_status() keeps its 6.18 sess_id form.
  Added (not upstream): release_async_work() clears cancel_fn/cancel_argv
  under request_lock, because synchronous CANCEL now calls cancel_fn on
  works found via conn->requests, which release_async_work() does not
  unlink.
  Not taken: the ksmbd_conn_cancel_async_requests() hunk (function absent),
  CHANGE_NOTIFY claim handling and the kerberos_expiry reset in logoff. ]
(cherry picked from commit d12168084c8c1b6d883c8eca5853929ac5136a9e)
